type: software
title: "Sharp finite-market prophet inequalities for a single threshold"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Exact worst-case values of a fixed threshold in random-order markets, and a proof of the Arnosti-Ma stockout conjecture. For independent, possibly heterogeneous values arriving in uniformly random order, the paper gives the exact worst-case ratio, at every finite market size, of a single static threshold that accepts the first k qualifiers against the average of the best l values: distribution-aware, calibrated to a stockout probability, calibrated to an expected utilisation, and for identical laws. The utilisation rule at its best target equals the distribution-aware optimum; the stockout rule loses an amount of exact order 1/n^2; identical laws are easier by order 1/n. Over all market sizes the stockout target proposed by Arnosti and Ma attains 1 - e^-k k^k/k!, which proves their conjecture, and the unequal-capacity constant of Molina et al. holds for heterogeneous values (static thresholds)."
